.TH BIGFLOATRECIPROCAL 3 "2026-09-21" "BigNums" "Library Functions Manual"
.nr HY 0
.ds AD l
.SH NAME
bigFloatReciprocal, bigFloatDiv, bigFloatSqrt \- compute a reciprocal, quotient, or square root
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include \(dqbignums.h\(dq
.sp
.BI "int bigFloatReciprocal(BigFloat *" "result" ","
.BI "    const BigFloat *" "x" ", int " "target_limbs" ");"
.sp
.BI "int bigFloatDiv(BigFloat *" "result" ", const BigFloat *" "a" ","
.BI "    const BigFloat *" "b" ", int " "target_limbs" ");"
.sp
.BI "int bigFloatSqrt(BigFloat *" "result" ", const BigFloat *" "x" ","
.BI "    int " "target_limbs" ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bigFloatReciprocal()
computes 1/x using scaled integer division.
.B bigFloatDiv()
computes a/b directly using scaled integer division.
.B bigFloatSqrt()
computes the nonnegative square root using an integer square-root algorithm.
Inputs must be initialized.  The output may alias either input.
.PP
All three functions clamp target_limbs to 1 through MAX_LIMBS (256).
Results are rounded toward zero to 32 * target_limbs significant binary bits,
up to 8192 bits.  Exact integer intermediates avoid approximation seeds and
intermediate mantissa overflow.  Division limits the final quotient as well.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 0 on success or INT_MAX if the normalized result's exponent cannot
be represented.  Reciprocal of zero and division by zero return INT_MAX.
Square root returns \-1 for a negative sign, including signed zero.
Positive zero succeeds.  Errors leave the output unchanged.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
BigFloat two, root;
bigFloatFromUint32(&two, 2);
if (bigFloatSqrt(&root, &two, 4) != 0)
    return 1;
printBigFloat(&root, 6);
.EE
.SH BUGS
Results use rounding toward zero, not rounding to nearest.
These routines cannot recover precision already lost in their inputs.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bigFloatTruncate (3),
.BR bigFloatMul (3),
.BR printBigFloat (3),
.BR bignums (3),
.BR bignums (7)
